  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Using a human centered-design to improve existing Child Labour Monitoring and Remediation System (CLMRS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project B aims to implement a series of interventions that seek to contribute to the prevention and reduction of child labor. These interventions are recommendations from Project A (impact assessment), which sought to delve deeper into the root causes of child labor in cocoa producing communities. To understand the effect of these new interventions on the prevalence of child labor and their potential for scaling up, ECOM will employ a robust impact assessment conducted by KIT Royal Tropical Institute. The interventions are structured around three pillars: (1)	Improving access to cost-saving, professionalised labor services for cocoa farming, (2)	Professionalising school committees in rural areas, and (3)	Supporting the development of income-generating activities among members of Village Savings and Loans Associations (VSLA) members.For the first pillar, ECOM will promote technical support and labor subsidies for cocoa farming households in communities at child labor risk. Services like pruning, compost manufacturing, mechanical weeding or application of phytosanitary products will be delivered by community labour groups that will be trained and equipped by ECOM with sustainable and innovative technologies (labor-saving tools).For the second pillar, ECOM will create and/or support school management committees (known as COGES in Cote d&apos;Ivoire) to manage the self-financing of school management related activities such as the canteen&#x2019;s supply of food, the improvement of the infrastructures, the support of children in difficulties (avoid immediate drop out of school) or the improvement or establishment of quality education initiatives like reading clubs or extra scholar activities.For the third and last pillar, the interventions aim at supporting VSLA members in communities with higher risk child labor in order to promote gender equity, children wellbeing and individual coaching on development of Income Generating Activities (IGA).</narrative>
  </description>
